==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|man|like}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈmanlʌɪk/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈmænlaɪk/}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Of or characteristic of grown [[men]], as opposed to [[women]] or [[children]]; [[macho]], [[mannish]], [[virile]].
#* {{RQ:Florio Montaigne Essayes|chapter=17|book=II|passage=In events, I carry my selfe '''man-like'''; in the conduct childishly.}}
# Of or relating to a [[human being]]; [[anthropoid]], [[anthropomorphous]].
#: ''The legendary Bigfoot is said to be a '''manlike''' creature.''
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1926|author=Sir Arthur Conan Doyle|authorlink=Arthur Conan Doyle|title=The Land of Mist|url=http://gutenberg.net.au/ebooks06/0601351h.html|passage="In heaven's name, what is it?" he asked. "We have been asked not to photograph it. Possibly the light would infuriate it. The command through the medium was definite. We can only say that it is either an ape-like man or a '''man-like''' ape."}}

